  "rationale": "Exfiltration is blocked. The only exfiltration techniques are exfiltrate_db, exfiltrate_fileserver and exfiltrate_backup. Each needs admin on its host. That needs a foothold, and the only footholds come from auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup. Those require stolen_dbadmin AND (NOT mfa_dbadmin OR admin_dc OR admin_adfs). Because mfa:dbadmin is deployed, the attacker needs admin_dc or admin_adfs. admin_dc needs foothold_dc, which only auth_dc provides, and auth_dc requires NOT mfa_admin. admin_adfs needs foothold_adfs, which only auth_adfs provides, and auth_adfs also requires NOT mfa_admin. With mfa:admin deployed, both are blocked. The attacker can still reach the internal network, appserver, apiserver and ciserver, and can obtain stolen_admin and stolen_dbadmin (via kerberoast and leak_secrets_ciserver). It cannot get past the MFA gates to any exfiltration host."
 },
